Kyuubi dependency repackaging
-----------------------------
Amoro removes the bundled org/slf4j/ classes from the distribution copy of
org.apache.kyuubi:kyuubi-hive-jdbc-shaded:1.10.2 to prevent its SLF4J 1.x API
from overriding the SLF4J 2.x API used by AMS. All retained upstream files,
including the original license and NOTICE records, remain unchanged.
The modified JAR carries META-INF/README-amoro-resource-changes. The original
Maven repository artifact is unchanged. Project: https://kyuubi.apache.org/.

JSP standard-resource replacements
----------------------------------
Five JSP schema/DTD resources, where present, are replaced with unmodified
GlassFish versions from commit 371c9e1beb285a30bd4203ec86fde5729dbd06f9,
under the selected CDDL-1.1 license. Resource paths and owner headers remain.
The copies in dependency JARs are modified during packaging; the original
Maven repository artifacts are unchanged. See LICENSE.jsp-resources and
LICENSE.CDDL-1.1 in the distribution's licenses directory (META-INF/licenses
in standalone fat JARs), and META-INF/README-amoro-resource-changes in the
modified JARs. Project: https://github.com/javaee/glassfish.

TLS packaging change
---------------------
The five statically linked netty-tcnative-boringssl native libraries are
removed from the modified ZooKeeper dependency copy and the runtime/fat
JARs. Netty Java code and unrelated epoll libraries remain. ZooKeeper uses
its default JDK TLS provider. Configurations explicitly setting
zookeeper.ssl.sslProvider=OPENSSL
must select JDK. Original producer license records remain as provenance.
See META-INF/README-amoro-resource-changes in modified JARs.

